From 11a967a71350fc877647c489c71a05a990d09cdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tstoltz <tristan.stoltz@evolvingresonantcocreationism.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 23:48:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add per-signature verified-observation API and experimental
 admission-hook settings

First slice of the admission-boundary experiment for nix-signature-policy
(see /srv/luminous-dynamics/nix-signature-policy). Adds:

- ValidPathInfo::checkSignaturesDetailed(): computes checkSignatures()'s
  existing valid-count AND the per-signature verified identity/algorithm
  observations an external authorization boundary needs, in one
  verification pass (not two independent passes -- avoids duplicated
  ML-DSA verification work and B/O drift). checkSignatures() is now a
  thin wrapper delegating to it; its behavior, including the
  content-addressed short-circuit, is unchanged. Each VerifiedSignature
  carries a stable signatureId (SHA-256 of the raw signature bytes) so
  exact-duplicate signatures share an ID without exposing raw bytes to
  callers that don't need them. Output is sorted by (keyName, keyType)
  for deterministic serialization. Documented explicitly as a bounded
  set of *positively verified* observations, not a complete per-signature
  pass/fail map -- unknown keys, invalid signatures, and malformed
  entries are omitted by design, not merely unimplemented.
- PublicKey::keyType() is pure virtual (not a throwing default), so a
  future or overlooked PublicKey subclass fails to build rather than
  verifying a signature and then throwing when asked what algorithm did
  the verifying. Confirmed via grep that nothing constructs a bare
  PublicKey. Implemented on Ed25519PublicKey and OpenSSLPublicKey
  (ML-DSA/ECDSA-P384).
- keyTypeProtocolName(KeyType): frozen wire strings (ed25519,
  ml-dsa-44/65/87, ecdsa-p384) matching the existing internal
  keyTypeMap and nix-signature-policy's own AlgorithmId strings --
  never serializes the enum's raw ordinal.
- Three new LocalStoreConfig settings gated behind a new experimental
  feature (Xp::ConfigurableSignatureAuthorization, off by default):
  signature-authorization-hook, signature-authorization-mode
  (legacy|conjunctive), signature-authorization-timeout-ms.

No admission behavior changes yet -- the settings are not consulted by
pathInfoIsUntrusted/addToStore yet (next step). Unset by default and
gated behind an off-by-default experimental feature, so this commit
alone changes nothing for any existing user.
